'' A program's own 'trycast' is called, not read as 'trycast( T, x )' (docs/tiko-interfaces
'' §5.5, §17 Q6): the parser checks KnownProc_, and Check keeps the user binding when the
'' first argument is no type reference.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/parser/src/trycast-user-proc.bas -o tests/parser/trycastuser.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/parser/trycastuser.exe
'' RUN: tests/parser/trycastuser.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  3
